## 3. Target Users & Jobs to Be Done

### Persona 1: The Reluctant Commuter (Primary)

**Profile:** Adult learner, 28–45, working professional. Has 10–15 minutes of fragmented time, often on a phone, with unreliable connectivity. Has started and abandoned Duolingo twice.

| Dimension | Job Statement |
|---|---|
| **Functional** | When I have a 10-minute gap between meetings, I want to review exactly the vocabulary that’s due for reinforcement, so I can make measurable progress without needing a full study session. |
| **Emotional** | When I miss a day of study, I want to return without feeling guilty or “behind,” so I can maintain momentum without streak-guilt mechanics. |
| **Social** | When I mention I’m learning Portuguese, I want to be able to point to a credible framework (CEFR) that signals I’m doing this seriously, not just playing a game. |

**Constraints:** Mobile-first, offline-capable, sessions under 10 minutes, no forced daily streaks.

**Evidence source:** Founder’s own experience + qualitative interviews (to be conducted).

---

### Persona 2: The Credential-Seeker (Secondary)

**Profile:** Adult learner, 25–40, studying Portuguese for a specific professional or academic milestone (e.g., job application requiring B1, university exchange at A2/B1). Needs demonstrable progress against a recognised standard.

| Dimension | Job Statement |
|---|---|
| **Functional** | When I’m preparing for a milestone that requires a specific CEFR level, I want to see exactly which Can-Do statements I’ve mastered and which remain, so I can focus my study time on the gaps. |
| **Emotional** | When I review my progress, I want to feel certain that my learning is real and measurable, not illusory activity. |
| **Social** | When I present my language ability to an employer or institution, I want to reference a structured CEFR-aligned record of what I can do, even if it’s not formally certified. |

**Constraints:** Needs CEFR-level dashboard, exportable Can-Do checklist, clear “next recommended node” guidance.

**Evidence source:** CEFR B2 is the most common employer requirement for professional roles (desk research).

---

### Anti-Persona: The Certification-Mill Student

**Profile:** Learner who wants only to pass a test with minimal learning, seeks answer keys, and would game any gamified system.

**Why named:** Explicitly excludes features optimised for completion metrics (e.g., streak mechanics, XP bonuses for speed over retention). The platform optimises for **genuine acquisition**, not engagement theatre.

