## 5. Current Workflows and Alternatives

| Alternative | What it does well | Where it falls short |
|---|---|---|
| **Duolingo** | Gamified, low friction, mobile-first | CEFR mapping opaque; progress measures activity, not proficiency; streak-guilt |
| **Anki + shared deck** | Powerful SRS, offline-capable | No CEFR guidance; setup overhead; no Can-Do mapping |
| **Traditional class** | Structured, teacher feedback | Fixed schedule; not self-paced; expensive |
| **Textbook + audio** | Authoritative content | No SRS; no progress tracking; not interactive |
| **Doing nothing** | Zero effort | No progress; eventual abandonment |

**Real competitor:** The most common alternative is **doing nothing** or **using a paper notebook**. The platform must offer a *lower-friction* path to structured progress than any of these.

