## Appendix: Key Concepts Reference

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **CEFR Node** | An abstract, language-independent unit of learning (e.g., “Can greet people and respond to greetings”). |
| **Realisation** | The language-specific expression of a CEFR node (vocabulary, grammar, examples) in a particular language. |
| **JTBD** | Jobs to Be Done: the functional, emotional, and social progress a user is trying to make in a given situation. |
| **SM-2** | A spaced repetition algorithm that schedules review intervals based on recall quality. |
| **Island** | An Astro concept: an interactive component hydrated on the client, isolated within an otherwise static page. |

